      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَّقٌ</span></b> , like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِمَّعٌ</span>, [in a copy of the JK incorrectly
written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَلِقٌ</span>,] <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَأَلِّقٌ</span> [<i>Shining, gleaming,</i> or
<i>glistening</i>]; (S, K;) applied to lightning. (JK.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also (assumed tropical:)  An <i>inconstant</i> man; from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">التَّأَلُّقُ</span> as
relating to lightning. (JK: there, in this instance,
written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَّقٌ</span>.)

